const page = { page: "lesson", paper: "paper-1", topic: "topic-2", unit: "2-3", lesson: "quran-and-sunnah" };
const title = "The Qur’an and the Sunnah · 2.3 · IGCSE Islamiyat";
const footerHtml = "Cambridge IGCSE Islamiyat 0493 &middot; Paper 1, Topic 2, Unit 2.3";
const mainHtml = "<section class=\"chapter\">\r\n      <div class=\"wrap\">\r\n        <div class=\"chapter-head\">\r\n          <h1>The Qur&rsquo;an and the Sunnah</h1>\r\n          <p class=\"ch-sub\">2.3 The Qur&rsquo;an in Legal Thinking &middot; why the Qur&rsquo;an leaves practical gaps for the Sunnah to fill</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p class=\"lede prose-col\">The previous lesson's prediction question asked where the missing detail of how to pray comes from. The Qur&rsquo;an states its own relationship to the Prophet's example directly:</p>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"pull\">\r\n          <span class=\"translation\">&ldquo;Whatever the Messenger has given you, take it; and whatever he has forbidden you, refrain from.&rdquo;</span>\r\n          <span class=\"cite\">Qur&rsquo;an 59:7</span>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p class=\"prose-col\">The gap between principle and practice is not an oversight &mdash; it is deliberate design. A book meant to be recited and revered as unchanging divine speech is not the ideal format for procedural detail that a living, breathing teacher can demonstrate, correct, and adapt in real time. The Prophet's own life &mdash; witnessed, memorised and passed on by thousands of companions &mdash; became the working manual for applying the Qur&rsquo;an's principles, which is exactly why the Hadith sciences you may study elsewhere in this course (isnad, matn, the classification into Sahih, Hasan and Da&rsquo;if) matter so much: a legal system built partly on Hadith is only as reliable as its verification of which hadiths are authentic.</p>\r\n\r\n        <div style=\"max-width:66ch; margin:40px auto 0;\" class=\"prose-col\">\r\n          <h3 style=\"display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap;\">Ready to practise?</h3>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-top:10px; color:var(--ink-soft);\">A short Practice Quiz first, then a graded Quiz once you're confident.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"lesson-pager\">\r\n          <a class=\"pager-link\" href=\"../four-sources-of-law/quiz.html\"><span class=\"pg-label\">&larr; Back</span><div class=\"pg-title\">The Four Sources of Law Quiz</div></a>\r\n          <a class=\"pager-link next\" href=\"practice.html\"><span class=\"pg-label\">Next &rarr;</span><div class=\"pg-title\">Practice Quiz</div></a>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>";
---

